    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2204.09934_rag::chunk_005</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2106.15561_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2106.15561_rag::chunk_012</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2110.12612_rag::chunk_008</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1705.10874_rag::chunk_018</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2110.12612_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1702.06378_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2106.12896_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mon-2-7-1_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1910.05453_rag::chunk_006</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1707.06065v1_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acoustic models generate acoustic features, from either linguistic features or characters/phonemes</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">(a.k.a. acoustic model) aims to generate prosodic attributes according to variance prediction</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">predict the acoustic features from linguistic features, which follow the paradigm of SPSS.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We mainly review the acoustic models according to different network structures such as RNN, CNN and Transformer</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a good tradeoff of the task difculties between the acoustic model and the HiFiNet vocoder</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">employing the enhanced speech obtained in the front end to re-train the pre-trained AM in the back-end</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the quality of the mel-spectrogram generated by acoustic model still has gap to recording due to the difculty of prosody modeling.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">multitask learning improves recognition accuracies of both SRNN and CTC acoustic models</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The resulting TTS model is comprised of two main components: 1) an acoustic model</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">applied to build the acoustic models for voice conversion</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">For decoding the emissions from the acoustic model on WSJ we use a lexicon as well as a separate language model</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acoustic model) aims to generate prosodic attributes according to variance prediction</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We use wav2letter as accoustic model (Collobert et al., 2016; 2019) and train for 1,000 epochs</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We use wav2letter as accoustic model (Collobert et al., 2016; 2019) and train for 1,000 epochs on 8 GPUs for both TIMIT and WSJ</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acoustic model needs to close the large gap between text and spectrogram</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acoustic model needs to close the large gap between text and spectrogram, such as duration, pitch, formant, voiced/unvoiced part, prosody, etc.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We apply our proposed DLN to deep bidirectional LSTM acoustic models</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
